FIX CHAMPIONSHIP crash (830): Sort_Leagues loop-bound Ghidra artifact (wild deref)

QA agent Finding: a Championship (race_type=4) race crashed the browser renderer when the player
drove -- silent (no WASM RuntimeError / console), reliably 3/3. Reproduced under native ASan via
a new DD2_CHAMP mode (runs the real Init_Wrecking_Championship -> Championship() path with
DD2_HOLD driving): SIGSEGV at a wild addr in FUN_0044c9c0 <- Sort_Leagues <- Championship.

Root = a Ghidra decompile artifact in Sort_Leagues @0x44c4b0. The asm loops EXACTLY 4 times:
  lea esi,[ebx+0x50]   ; esi = &local_5c[20]
  ...call FUN_0044c9c0(piVar3,5); add ebx,0x14; cmp ebx,esi; jne
i.e. 4 leagues x 5 = 20 cars, piVar3 stepping +5 ints from local_5c[0] to local_5c[20]. Ghidra
mis-rendered the loop bound `&local_5c[20]` as the bogus stack address `(int *)&stack0xfffffff4`
(and invented a phantom `int aiStackY_c005c[196606]`). So the loop ran far past local_5c[20],
handing FUN_0044c9c0 uninitialized stack ints as car indices -> `iVar6*0x36 + 0x93deee` wild
pointer -> crash. Fixed the bound to `local_5c + 20` and dropped the phantom array. Same
decompile-artifact class as the scattered-locals / mis-typed-symbol fixes.

Native repro DD2_CHAMP now runs the championship past the standings sort. verify + verify-wasm
10/10 both; native<->wasm L9 702/702 bit-identical (Sort_Leagues is championship-only, not in
the attract path).
--- a/dd2.c
+++ b/dd2.c
@@ -38220,7 +38220,6 @@
   int iVar1;
   int iVar2;
   int *piVar3;
-  int aiStackY_c005c [196606];
   int local_5c [20];
   
   iVar2 = 0;
@@ -38235,7 +38234,7 @@
   do {
     FUN_0044c9c0(piVar3,5);
     piVar3 = piVar3 + 5;
-  } while (piVar3 != (int *)&stack0xfffffff4);
+  } while (piVar3 != local_5c + 20);   /* asm 0x44c4f7: cmp ebx,esi where esi=&local_5c[20] (4 leagues x5=20 cars); Ghidra mis-rendered the bound as &stack0xfffffff4 -> ran far past local_5c -> read stack garbage as car indices -> wild deref crash in FUN_0044c9c0 (championship standings) */
   return;
 }
 
